{# goal: Convert the removed-to-retained signal mapping into explicit Lean propositions proving finite verification-graph coverage preservation without claiming runtime effectiveness. #}
[inference]
contract:
  input:
    baseline_graph: object
    candidate_graph: object
    lean_binary: string
  output:
    graph_gate_status: string
    generated_proof_path: string
    lean_status: string
    negative_control_status: string
    proof_scope: object
    empirical_residual: array
visibility: Public
---

[inference]
temperature = 0.0
work_effort = "high"
verbosity = "detailed"
thinking_budget = "full"

Use the deterministic current graph gate to generate Lean 4 obligations.

Observed baseline graph (the sole source of required keys):
```json
{{ baseline_graph | tojson }}
```
Candidate graph with retained rows and removed-to-retained mappings:
```json
{{ candidate_graph | tojson }}
```
Lean executable: {{ lean_binary }}

The candidate graph must retain exactly the baseline `required` and `before`
arrays. Call `generate-verification-preservation-proof.sh` on the candidate
JSON artifact to validate complete five-field signals, exact required set,
retained artifacts, and all removed mappings; it emits the Lean source, not
the model. The receipt checker regenerates the proof and compares it to the
supplied file. Run the named Lean binary, capture the output and version,
and run `test-generate-verification-preservation-proof.sh` with that binary;
a missing-signal instance must fail. No `sorry`, axioms, or unsafe escape.
The proof does not establish runtime oracle quality, fault realism, I/O,
or timing; preserve these empirical checks independently.

Return JSON only:
```json
{
  "graph_gate_status":"passed|failed",
  "generated_proof_path":"path returned by deterministic generator",
  "lean_status":"compiled|failed|unavailable",
  "negative_control_status":"missing-signal rejected|failed|unavailable",
  "proof_scope": {
    "proves":["finite declared five-field signal coverage preservation"],
    "does_not_prove":["runtime oracle quality","fault realism","timing improvement"]
  },
  "empirical_residual": []
}
```